    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d64">

                <pb facs="0132" n="52" sameAs="frus:frus1901/pg52"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Squiers to Mr.
                            Hay.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Pekin</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1901-04-22"><hi rendition="#italic">April 22,
                        1901</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 614.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to inclose a copy of a
                    proclamation, dated April 18, issued by the German consul-general of Tientsin,
                    by which notification is given that the German concession there has been, by the
                    consent of the Chinese authorities, extended as indicated on the map<anchor
                        n="a" xml:id="d64-f1"/> inclosed herewith.</p>
                <p>I have not instructed Mr. Ragsdale to enter a protest against this action, as it
                    does not appear that the interests of any of our nationals are involved or in
                    any way prejudiced.</p>
                <p>The inclosed map also shows the extensions of old concessions, as well as new
                    concessions up to date.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">H. G. Squiers.</hi></signed></closer>


                <xi:include href="d64-a1.xml" xpointer="d64-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
